### FirstClub Membership — demo script (IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client)
### Run top-to-bottom against a running app (./mvnw spring-boot:run).
### Plan/tier ids below match the default seed (Monthly=1, Quarterly=2, Yearly=3;
### Silver=1, Gold=2, Platinum=3).

@base = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Browse plans
GET {{base}}/api/plans

### 2. Browse tiers (benefits + qualifying criteria)
GET {{base}}/api/tiers

### 3. Create a user
POST {{base}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Asha", "cohort": null }

> {% client.global.set("userId", response.body.id); %}

### 4. Subscribe to Yearly + Gold (charges base fee + Gold joining fee)
POST {{base}}/api/users/{{userId}}/subscription
Content-Type: application/json

{ "planId": 3, "tierId": 2 }

> {% client.global.set("subscriptionId", response.body.subscriptionId); %}

### 5. View membership (note progressToNextTier = Platinum)
GET {{base}}/api/users/{{userId}}/membership

### 6. Five fulfilled orders this month (event-driven activity accrual)
POST {{base}}/api/orders/events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": {{userId}}, "amount": 1000 }

### (repeat the order event a few times to cross Gold's ORDER_COUNT >= 5)
POST {{base}}/api/orders/events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": {{userId}}, "amount": 1000 }

###
POST {{base}}/api/orders/events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": {{userId}}, "amount": 1000 }

###
POST {{base}}/api/orders/events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": {{userId}}, "amount": 1000 }

###
POST {{base}}/api/orders/events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": {{userId}}, "amount": 1000 }

### 7. Membership again — progress now reflects the 5 orders / 5000 spend
GET {{base}}/api/users/{{userId}}/membership

### 8. Settle the current month — Gold criteria met, so the fee is WAIVED (tier kept free)
POST {{base}}/api/admin/tiering/run

### 9. Active benefits for the user
GET {{base}}/api/users/{{userId}}/benefits

### 10. Preview benefits on a cart (free delivery + 5% off applied)
POST {{base}}/api/users/{{userId}}/benefits/preview
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cartTotal": 2000, "deliveryFee": 50 }

### ----- Difference-fee path -----

### 11. Upgrade to Platinum (pay joining fee)
POST {{base}}/api/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/upgrade
Content-Type: application/json

{ "targetTierId": 3 }

### 12. Settle a fresh month with no activity — owes the Platinum-minus-free difference
POST {{base}}/api/admin/tiering/run?period=2026-07

### 13. Find the outstanding invoice (captures paymentId of the FEE_INVOICED settlement)
GET {{base}}/api/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/settlements

> {%
    for (let s of response.body) {
        if (s.status === "FEE_INVOICED") { client.global.set("paymentId", s.paymentId); }
    }
%}

### 14. Pay the fee within the grace window → Platinum retained
POST {{base}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/confirm

### 15. Membership stays Platinum
GET {{base}}/api/users/{{userId}}/membership

### ----- Grace-expiry downgrade path -----

### 16. Set grace window to 0 days (runtime config change, no restart)
PUT {{base}}/api/admin/policy
Content-Type: application/json

{ "graceWindowDays": 0 }

### 17. Settle another fresh month → fee invoiced with an already-passed deadline
POST {{base}}/api/admin/tiering/run?period=2026-08

### 18. Sweep expired grace → unpaid Platinum settles down to the free-eligible tier
POST {{base}}/api/admin/tiering/grace-sweep

### 19. Membership now shows the downgraded tier
GET {{base}}/api/users/{{userId}}/membership

### ----- Runtime configurability demo -----

### 20. Retune Gold's order-count threshold live (admin CRUD, no redeploy)
PUT {{base}}/api/admin/tiers/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Gold",
  "rank": 1,
  "joiningFee": 499,
  "monthlyFee": 199,
  "active": true,
  "criteriaCombinator": "ANY",
  "benefits": [
    { "type": "FREE_DELIVERY", "description": "Free delivery on all orders" },
    { "type": "EXTRA_DISCOUNT_PERCENT", "value": 7, "description": "7% extra off" }
  ],
  "criteria": [
    { "type": "ORDER_COUNT", "operator": "GTE", "threshold": 3 },
    { "type": "COHORT", "stringValue": "VIP" }
  ]
}

### ----- Subscription expiry -----

### 21. Expire lapsed subscriptions (daily job also does this automatically).
### API-created subscriptions always expire in the future, so to see a non-zero result
### first backdate a row's expiry_date in the H2 console (/h2-console), then run this.
POST {{base}}/api/admin/subscriptions/expire-due
